{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012sjF3upzVM2RYi1PF3Dw6g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment data for the \"worst\" tier, for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan. I need to carefully consider the worst-tier definition and produce predicted results with rationales.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n\n**Worst tier meaning:**\n- Only exposure DAG shows direction reversal, all other 5 topologies are monotonic\n- OR ASV monotonicity fails in some topology needing repair\n- Core assumptions: mediation/collider/M-bias/instrument/front-door have no direction reversal under non-differential K≥3; all non-exposure topologies behave like confounding (predictable direction, magnitude varies with C structure); ASV monotonicity may fail in 1 topology (like collider); empirical confusion matrices are diagonal-dominant, extreme C structures rare; correction framework degenerates to \"use MLA\" in most scenarios\n\n\n- Now I'm setting the expected metric ranges for worst-tier scenarios: reversal_topologies_count stays at exactly 1, mediation and collider violations remain absent, theory-MC alignment drops to 70-85%, ASV coverage at nominal 95% falls to 80-88%, formal proof sharpness is minimal at 1-2 proofs, binarization effects stay small at 5-10% max delta, and correction framework accuracy mirrors the theory-MC match at 70-85%.\n\nThe key insight here is that direction reversals are concentrated specifically in exposure misclassification—a critical finding since exposure is typically the LLM-annotated variable in CSS studies. Other DAG topologies show predictable direction but their magnitude varies widely and can't be reliably predicted from binary sensitivity and specificity alone. This reveals a topology-dependent dichotomy that changes how I frame the findings.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the experimental roadmap: starting with deriving and validating bias expressions across 6 DAG topologies with K=3, then extending to larger K values with matrix notation and interpretability tools. I'll need empirical confusion matrices from 3 LLMs across 3 CSS tasks, analyze binarization collapse patterns, develop formal ASV proofs for confounding/mediation/collider cases, validate ASV through Monte Carlo for more complex topologies, calibrate ASV on real data, build a correction guidance framework, examine pathological confusion matrices, and create a Python toolkit for annotation sensitivity analysis.\n\nFor the worst-case tier, I need to be precise about what actually reverses—only the exposure DAG shows direction reversal.  The other five topologies (mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door) maintain consistent direction. I'm expecting theory-MC match rates around 0.7-0.85 since some expressions may have edge-case mismatches, ASV coverage at 95% nominal will likely fall to 0.80-0.88 due to under-coverage, only 1-2 topologies will get full sharpness proofs, binarization effects will be more modest at 0.05-0.10 delta, and empirical ASV concordance will land somewhere in the 3-6 range.\n\nWriting YAML specifications... done (MVP), monotonic toward OVB, no reversal\n- Exposure: already done (MVP), strong reversal (85% violation, 83.4% sign reversal)\n- Mediation: worst tier → 0% violation rate, monotonic, direction predictable\n- Collider: worst tier → 0% violation rate, but collider bias behavior may be interesting\n- M-bias: 0% violation, monotonic\n- Instrument: 0% violation, monotonic\n- Front-door: 0% violation, monotonic\n- theory_mc_match: 0.7-0.85 range → some structures have mismatches, so roughly 25-31 out of 36 configurations are matching, with more complex topologies like M-bias and front-door potentially having expression mismatches due to higher-order interaction terms.\n\nFor plan_002 with K=5,7, the matrix expressions are derived but hard to interpret, eigendecomposition handles confounding and mediation well but struggles with collider, and the worst-case bounds are conservative by a factor of 2-3x. Plan_003's empirical results show diagonal-dominant confusion matrices as expected, though the limited extreme structures make it hard to demonstrate ASV's practical value, and inter-model correlation stays moderate. Plan_008's binarization shows smaller deltas (0.05-0.10) compared to MVP's 0.103, with some topologies showing less dramatic effects.\n\nFor plan_004, formal proofs establish monotonicity for confounding and possibly mediation, but only 1-2 topologies achieve sharpness, collider might violate monotonicity requiring a modified ASV definition, and coverage sits at 0.80-0.88 at 95% nominal indicating under-coverage. Plan_005 relies on MC validation for the remaining three topologies, with one potentially having monotonicity issues. Plan_006's empirical ASV shows concordance in only 3-6 out of 9 task-LLM combinations, with diagonal-dominant matrices producing large or vacuous ASVs. Plan_007's correction framework achieves 0.7-0.85 accuracy but many scenarios default to \"use MLA\" and the decision tree lacks discrimination. Plan_009 examines pathological cases.\n\nFor plan_009, spectral analysis reveals the reversal mechanism for exposure while other topologies show less dramatic findings. Plan_010's toolkit is functional but the empirical matrices don't provide compelling demonstration value.\n\nNow I'm diving deeper into the theory-MC match rate, which ranges from 0.7 to 0.85 across all topologies. The MVP structures (confounding and exposure) achieved perfect matches, but when I account for the remaining four topologies with six C structures each, the overall rate suggests roughly 17 out of 24 new tests have mismatches, likely stemming from approximation issues in certain structures. So across all 36 topology and C-structure combinations, I'm breaking down where the theoretical predictions match the Monte Carlo results. The MVP covers the simpler cases—confounding and exposure structures validate cleanly—but the newer topologies show degradation as complexity increases. Mediation loses one structure to higher-order terms, collider and M-bias each drop two due to non-linearities and approximation errors, instrumental variables struggles with misclassification, and front-door is the hardest with only half matching, since it chains multiple mediation-like mechanisms together. Writing YAML output...\n\nThe mismatches aren't random—they cluster in topologies with compound structures, suggesting the closed-form theory has real approximation limits rather than just Monte Carlo noise, which is concerning for the worst-performing tiers.\n\nFor the worst tier results, the simpler topologies like confounding and mediation have exact expressions that match well, but complex ones like collider conditioning and front-door with compound mediation break down at extreme C structures where higher-order terms dominate. The 70-85% match rate reflects genuine algebraic difficulty in those edge cases.\n\nNow I'm organizing this into the YAML format and noting that the empirical confusion matrices show limited practical concordance for the worst tier, with only 3-6 cases matching across the ASV demonstrations.\n\nWriting comprehensive YAML output... able direction\" because the misclassification matrix operates on a variable that doesn't directly define the treatment contrast. Exposure misclassification is special because it directly scrambles treatment assignment labels — when K≥3, this scrambling can map treatment A's outcomes onto treatment B's estimates, causing reversal. For confounders/mediators/colliders, the misclassification affects a variable that modulates bias magnitude but doesn't directly swap effect numerator/denominator.\n\nWhy theory-MC mismatches? For collider/M-bias/front-door, the closed-form expressions involve conditioning (collider), multiple confounding paths (M-bias), or chained mediation (front-door). At extreme C structures, these expressions' first-order Taylor approximations lose accuracy. The mismatches are systematic (always at extreme C) not random.\n\n**plan_002**: K=5,7 matrix expressions + interpretability\n\nFor larger K values, the eigendecomposition becomes harder to interpret — confounding and mediation show clean spectral structure with a dominant mode capturing most bias variance, but collider and M-bias scenarios require multiple eigenvectors to explain the pattern. The worst-case bounds end up being conservative (2-3x looser than needed) because they must cover adversarial misclassification structures that rarely materialize in real data.\n\n**plan_003**: Empirical confusion matrices\n\nThe confusion matrices I'm generating show diagonal dominance with accuracy ranging from 0.65 to 0.85, indicating most classifications stay correct even under misclassification. The monotonicity argument holds for confounding and mediation cases—more error amplifies the bias mechanism—but collider behavior breaks this pattern since conditioning on a misclassified collider introduces non-linear bias that doesn't scale monotonically with error magnitude, suggesting ASV might need refinement for that topology. The coverage shortfall stems from ASV bounds being overly pessimistic for some structures while underestimating collider effects, leaving the bounds either too loose or too tight depending on the DAG.\n\nNow I'm realizing the coverage numbers actually indicate under-coverage—at 80-88% instead of the nominal 95%, the bounds are too tight and missing the true bias more often than they should. This could stem from approximation errors between the closed-form theory and Monte Carlo results, the δ-ball parametrization not capturing all relevant perturbation directions, or non-monotonicity in certain topologies preventing the maximum from appearing at the boundary.\n\nThe under-coverage is concentrated in the complex topologies like front-door, M-bias, and collider where the theory-MC mismatch is most pronounced and the bias expressions themselves are approximate. For the simpler topologies—confounding, exposure, mediation—coverage runs closer to nominal around 92-94%. So the aggregate 80-88% is being pulled down by these problematic cases.\n\nLooking at the remaining three topologies to validate: M-bias shows monotonicity but fails on sharpness since the actual maximum isn't achieved by the bound, while instrument and front-door maintain monotonicity though front-door has violations at the extremes. The M-bias case is particularly tricky because the dual-confounder structure means the true maximum doesn't align with where the ASV bound predicts it.\n\nNow examining the empirical ASV calibration, I'm seeing that only 3-6 out of 9 task-LLM combinations have finite ASVs, with the rest being vacuous because the confusion matrices are so diagonal-dominant. When the ASV is actually finite though, it does correctly flag which combinations are robust.\n\nFor the correction guidance framework, the decision tree is collapsing into recommending MLA across 60-70% of scenarios since it's the most universally applicable method when you have a confusion matrix estimate and adequate data.  The 15-30% of exceptions where alternatives like gold-label collection, IV-specific correction, or PPI might be better are edge cases involving exposure misclassification with direction reversal or specific finite-sample advantages. The 0.70-0.85 accuracy reflects that many recommendations are practically equivalent to just using MLA anyway.\n\nFor binarization effects, the worst-tier topologies show much smaller deltas (0.05-0.10) compared to the MVP's 0.103, with some configurations barely responding to binarization at all.  The difference hinges on whether the folded variable preserves the main causal pathway — symmetric roles like mediation and instruments lose less information, while exposure and collider topologies suffer asymmetric information loss. This validates that binarization is inadequate but doesn't produce the dramatic failure I was hoping for.\n\nNow examining the spectral properties of the confusion matrices to understand the exposure reversal mechanism more clearly. The toolkit's real limitation is that direction reversal detection—the most interesting finding—only matters for exposure topology, while other topologies just get uncertainty quantification, which is correct but uninspiring for demonstration purposes. The empirical results from plan_003 show mostly diagonal-dominant matrices where the toolkit safely reports low risk across topologies, which is accurate but not compelling for a demo. Now I'm thinking through what tables and figures each experiment would generate—plan_001 needs a topology comparison table with reversal rates and bias statistics, plus heatmaps and scatter plots showing theoretical versus Monte Carlo bias across configurations. For plan_002, I'm starting to map out the eigendecomposition summaries for different K values.\n\nGenerating experiment tables and figures... Writing YAML config... Now I'm seeing that the exposure topology is the only one showing reversals across the random search, while all other causal structures remain stable. Looking at the eigenvalue decomposition for plan_002, K=5 gives cleaner concentration of bias variance compared to K=7, which becomes too dispersed and produces overly conservative bounds. For plan_003, I'm checking the protest event coding accuracy with Llama 4 Maverick at 0.71.\n\nComparing model performance across the three tasks—protest event coding, stance detection, and toxicity classification—with their respective diagonal dominance ratios showing how well-structured each model's error patterns are. The inter-model error correlation of 0.58 suggests moderate agreement in where these models fail.\n\nLooking at downstream bias relative to gold standard labels, most combinations stay within statistical noise, though stance detection with lower-accuracy models shows slightly elevated bias. The formal proofs for confounding adjustment in plan_004 establish monotonicity and sharpness, with empirical coverage rates hovering near nominal levels across different confidence thresholds.\n\nHowever, the mediation and collider adjustments reveal significant limitations: mediation's bound is overly conservative by a factor of 1.4–1.8, and collider adjustment fails monotonicity for about 7% of causal structures around δ=0.3–0.5, leading to undercoverage at 95% nominal. Only the confounding case achieves a formal sharpness proof, suggesting I need to either restrict the collider ASV to monotone δ-paths or develop a conditional variant to handle the non-monotone regions. Looking at the performance across all six topologies, the M-bias and Instrument approaches are holding up well with monotonicity validated and coverage around 0.86-0.88, while Front-door is lagging at 0.79 despite maintaining monotonicity in most scenarios. The weighted average across all topologies comes to about 0.87, which is slightly above my earlier target.\n\nI need to dial back the Front-door and Collider coverage values to land within the acceptable range, so I'm adjusting those down to 0.76 and 0.78 respectively, which brings the overall average to 0.85 and fits nicely within the bounds. Now for plan_006, I'm testing how well ASV predictions align with actual robustness across nine different task-LLM combinations, checking whether ASV correctly identifies which ones are fragile versus stable across the relevant DAG topologies.\n\nThe concordance metric here is really about counting how many combinations have ASVs that are actually informative rather than trivially large—so out of the nine combinations, I'm expecting around 4 to have meaningful ASV values that genuinely discriminate between robust and fragile cases, while the other 5 would have such clean confusion matrices that ASV can't really tell us anything useful. Moving on to plan_007, I'm now looking at how different topologies interact with various error structures.\n\nFor plan_007, the framework achieves 78% accuracy across the Monte Carlo scenarios, with exposure topology cases performing well when recommending gold label collection or acknowledging when correction isn't feasible. The confounding and mediation cases tend toward MLA recommendations, which is somewhat obvious to any experienced researcher. The trickier cases are collider and M-bias scenarios where the framework sometimes recommends PPI when MLA might be better or vice versa, and these mismatches are dragging down the overall accuracy. About two-thirds of all recommendations end up being MLA anyway.\n\nFor plan_008, I'm now examining how the maximum Δ values change across different K values, starting with K=3 where the maximum difference is around 0.089 for the confounding topology. from MVP-like scenario) — wait, the range is [0.05, 0.10]\n  - Actually, across ALL topologies:\n    - Confounding K=3: Δ = 0.089 (close to MVP's 0.103 but slightly different because of different C structure sampling)\n    - Exposure K=3: Δ = 0.072 (binarization of exposure has different effect)\n    - Mediation K=3: Δ = 0.041\n    - Collider K=3: Δ = 0.068\n    - M-bias K=3: Δ = 0.055\n    - Instrument K=3: Δ = 0.038\n    - Front-door K=3: Δ = 0.045\n  - K=5: generally larger Δ because more information lost, maxing out around 0.095\n  - K=7: peaks at 0.098\n\nSo the overall maximum across all topologies and K values is 0.098, which fits within the [0.05, 0.10] range. But this is actually less dramatic than the MVP's 0.103 for confounding K=3, which is disappointing since we're testing all six topologies systematically now. The worst-tier maximum of 0.08 is lower than what we saw before, likely because the systematic sampling approach differs from the MVP's specific structure choices. MVP's 0.103 was for a specific near-permutation C structure that happened to be extreme. The systematic search across topologies finds that confounding DAG is actually where the largest binarization effect occurs, with other topologies showing smaller effects.\n\nThere's a discrepancy between the plan description saying 0.089 for confounding DAG K=3 and the MVP metrics showing 0.103 as the max. Looking at the YAML, the binarization_max_delta for plan_008 is 0.05-0.10 across all six topologies systematically, which makes sense—the worst tier max is around 0.08, mostly driven by confounding and exposure topologies, while others contribute lower deltas. This is consistent with the MVP's 0.103 for confounding, suggesting binarization is less problematic in other topologies than initially hoped.\n\nFor plan_009, the spectral analysis reveals a clear mechanism: exposure reversal happens when the eigenvalue ratio λ₂/λ₁ of C exceeds roughly 0.6 for K=3.\n\nThe spectral gap itself predicts bias direction with high accuracy around 0.92 AUC, and there's an even simpler proxy—diagonal dominance below 0.45 reliably indicates reversal. Other topologies show only monotone relationships between the largest eigenvalue and bias magnitude with no directional reversals, and block-diagonal structures create magnitude variations but no sign flips.\n\nFor plan_010, the toolkit is functional and pip-installable with six worked examples covering each topology, though the empirical results limit how compelling the demonstration is. The API takes a DAG, confounding structure, and estimate to output the bias expression, asymptotic variance, and correction recommendation, running in under a second for K≤7 and under ten seconds for K≤15.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the YAML configuration.\n\nI need to be precise about what the tables and figures would actually contain rather than being vague. For plan_003, the API cost estimate sits around $300-550 depending on annotation complexity, though that's more of a logistical detail than a results prediction.\n\nWriting the complete YAML specification... Writing YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10917,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10917},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd93169f-899b-425b-835b-3968c6801b13","uuid":"1496ca9f-9fb7-4410-aa91-b635d3c12731"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012sjF3upzVM2RYi1PF3Dw6g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Version B framing. Lead finding: \"multi-class annotation error 的危险性是 topology-dependent 的：\n  exposure misclassification 在方向和幅度上均不可预测，其余拓扑方向可预测但幅度需全 K×K 矩阵\n  才能量化——binary 框架在两种情况下均不足。\" Claim 1 从 \"breaks guarantees across topologies\"\n  调整为 \"reveals a sharp topology-dependent dichotomy\"——exposure 是唯一方向不可预测的拓扑，\n  这本身是重要发现（exposure 是 CSS 中最常被 LLM 标注的变量）。Claim 2 的 ASV 从\n  \"robustness to direction reversal\" 调整为 \"robustness to magnitude uncertainty\"，\n  因 collider ASV 单调性部分失效（7% violations），需修改定义或加条件，降低紧性要求。\n  Claim 3 权重增加——correction guidance 的实用价值成为主要卖点，弥补 taxonomy 发现不够 dramatic。\n  需额外投入：(a) spectral 分析深挖 exposure 反转机制（λ₂/λ₁ 阈值），\n  (b) 经验实验扩充至 4-5 个 task 以补偿理论贡献缩窄，\n  (c) 考虑 user study 展示 ASV 对研究者决策的影响。\n  theory-MC match 在复杂拓扑（front-door, collider）偏低，需坦诚承认闭合形式表达式的近似局限性，\n  将 MC 验证本身作为补充贡献。经验混淆矩阵 diagonal-dominant，极端 C 结构罕见——\n  ASV 在多数实证场景输出 \"robust\"，实用区分力有限，需通过 semi-synthetic 注入实验补救。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Six-topology bias taxonomy (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: |\n      对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）\n      推导 K=3 闭合形式 bias 表达式，用 MC 验证（1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 种 C 结构）。\n      核心问题：哪些拓扑在 non-differential K≥3 误分类下出现方向反转？\n    expected_results:\n      reversal_topologies_count: 1\n      confounding_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      confounding_theory_mc_match: \"6/6\"\n      confounding_bias_range: \"0.063–0.298\"\n      exposure_reversal_rate: 0.85\n      exposure_sign_reversal_rate: 0.834\n      exposure_amplification_rate: 0.141\n      exposure_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      exposure_bias_range: \"-0.84–0.42\"\n      mediation_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      mediation_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      mediation_bias_range: \"0.00–0.15\"\n      collider_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      collider_theory_mc_match: \"4/6\"\n      collider_bias_range: \"0.02–0.18\"\n      mbias_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      mbias_theory_mc_match: \"4/6\"\n      mbias_bias_range: \"0.04–0.22\"\n      instrument_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      instrument_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      instrument_bias_range: \"0.03–0.25\"\n      frontdoor_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      frontdoor_theory_mc_match: \"3/6\"\n      frontdoor_bias_range: \"0.01–0.19\"\n      overall_theory_mc_match: \"32/42 (0.76)\"\n      random_100k_reversal_topologies: \"exposure only\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst 档的核心预测：仅 exposure DAG 出现方向反转。机制上，exposure misclassification\n      直接扰乱 treatment assignment labels——当 K≥3 时，near-permutation C 导致 label swap，\n      将 treatment A 的 outcome 映射到 treatment B 的估计上，产生符号翻转。这在 K=2 时\n      结构性不可能（binary 只有\"正确/错误\"两种状态，non-differential 保证 bias toward null）。\n      其余 5 个拓扑中，misclassified 变量（confounder/mediator/collider/instrument/front-door variable）\n      不直接定义 treatment contrast，其误分类调制 bias magnitude 但不翻转 numerator/denominator，\n      因此方向可预测。Theory-MC match 率 0.76 偏低的原因：collider（conditioning 引入非线性）、\n      M-bias（双 confounder 路径交互）、front-door（复合 mediation 步骤）的闭合形式表达式\n      在 extreme C structures 下需要高阶 Taylor 项，一阶近似不够精确。Front-door 最差（3/6），\n      因为 front-door criterion 涉及两步 mediation，每步的近似误差在复合后被放大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Six-Topology Bias Taxonomy Summary (K=3)\"\n        description: |\n          6 rows (topologies) × columns: reversal_rate_100k, named_structure_match (x/6),\n          bias_range [min, max], bias_direction_class (monotonic-toward-null / monotonic-toward-OVB /\n          unpredictable), mechanism_summary.\n          Key pattern: exposure 行显著异于其余——reversal 85%，direction unpredictable；\n          其余 5 行 reversal 0%，方向可预测，但 magnitude range 差异大\n          （confounding 0.06-0.30 vs mediation 0.00-0.15 vs collider 0.02-0.18）。\n      - name: \"Table 2: Theory vs MC Bias — Per-Structure Detail\"\n        description: |\n          42 rows (6 topologies × ~7 structures including identity-adjacent, uniform-leaning,\n          near-permutation, block-diagonal, asymmetric, random-moderate, plus MVP-inherited).\n          Columns: topology, C_structure, theoretical_bias, mc_mean, mc_95ci, match (✓/✗).\n          10 个 ✗ 集中在 collider-near-permutation, mbias-block-diagonal,\n          frontdoor-near-permutation/asymmetric/block-diagonal。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Heatmap — topology (y) × C-structure (x)，color = signed bias magnitude。Exposure 行出现蓝红交替（正负 bias），其余行单色渐变（单调）。最直观的 'dichotomy' 可视化。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter — theoretical bias (x) vs MC mean bias (y)，per topology color-coded。理想 y=x 线上 confounding/exposure 点紧贴，front-door 点偏离最大。附 R² per topology。\"\n      - \"Fig 3: 100k random C density plot — per topology 的 bias distribution。Exposure 双峰分布（正负），其余单峰。\"\n    analysis: |\n      核心结论：topology-dependent dichotomy 成立但 dramatic 程度有限。Exposure 是唯一 \"dangerous\"\n      拓扑，其余 5 个是 \"well-behaved\"。这支持 Version B framing，但问题是 5 个 well-behaved\n      拓扑的故事不够 exciting——\"magnitude varies but direction is predictable\" 比\n      \"guarantees break\" 弱得多。Theory-MC mismatch 在复杂拓扑的存在是双刃剑：一方面暴露\n      闭合表达式的局限性（reviewer concern），另一方面 MC 验证本身成为必要贡献\n      （\"我们提供的不仅是理论，还有数值验证\"）。Front-door 3/6 match 可能需要在论文中\n      降格为 \"MC-validated conjecture\" 而非 \"theorem\"。\n      Version B lead: 虽然 5 个拓扑方向可预测，但 magnitude range 的跨拓扑差异\n      （confounding 0.06-0.30 vs mediation 0.00-0.15）本身有信息量——研究者需要知道\n      自己的 DAG topology 处于哪个 magnitude regime，binary 框架无法提供这个信息。\n\n  - name: \"General-K matrix expressions and interpretability (K=5,7)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: |\n      将 bias 表达式推广到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式，开发三个可解释性工具：\n      (a) eigendecomposition 摘要，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\n      在 confounding + mediation + collider 上验证。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.82\n      confounding_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.76\n      mediation_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.75\n      mediation_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.68\n      collider_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.58\n      collider_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.49\n      K5_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.70\n      K7_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.63\n      worst_case_bound_tightness_K5: \"1.8–2.5x conservative\"\n      worst_case_bound_tightness_K7: \"2.5–3.2x conservative\"\n      modes_needed_for_90pct_variance_collider_K7: 4\n    result_rationale: |\n      K 增大时，C 的自由度从 K=3 的 6 个增长到 K=5 的 20 个、K=7 的 42 个。\n      Confounding DAG 的 bias 有简单的方向结构（residual confounding 沿单一方向累积），\n      因此 dominant eigenvalue 即使在 K=7 仍捕获 76% variance——eigendecomposition 是有效的摘要工具。\n      Collider DAG 的 bias 来自 conditioning 引入的伪相关，其方向依赖于 collider 各类别间的\n      相对误分类强度——K=7 时 7 个类别的两两误分类形成多维度干扰，dominant eigenvalue 仅捕获\n      49%，需要 4 个 mode 才能解释 90% variance，eigendecomposition 失去摘要价值。\n      Worst-case bounds 松的原因：bounds 必须覆盖 adversarial C 结构，但实际 C 的 feasible region\n      在高 K 时是高维空间中的低维 manifold——bounds 优化的 supremum 在实践中不可达。\n      Theory-MC match 在 K=7 降至 0.63，因为矩阵形式表达式中的 Kronecker product 项\n      在数值求解时积累舍入误差，且 MC 的 N=10000 在 K=7 时 per-cell 样本量不足\n      （7×7=49 cells，某些 cell 可能 <50 observations）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Eigendecomposition Summary — K=3,5,7 × 3 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows (3 K × 3 topologies) × columns: K, topology, λ₁/tr(Λ), modes_for_90pct,\n          dominant_mode_interpretation, bound_tightness_ratio.\n          Key pattern: confounding 始终 clean（1-2 modes），collider 随 K 增长迅速恶化。\n      - name: \"Table 4: Worst-Case Scalar Bound vs Actual MC Maximum Bias\"\n        description: |\n          展示 bound 的 conservativeness。Columns: topology, K, worst_case_bound,\n          mc_observed_max, ratio. Ratio 从 K=3 的 1.3x 增长到 K=7 的 3.2x。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Eigenvalue spectrum bar chart — 3 panels (K=3,5,7)，每 panel 3 条 bar groups (topologies)，bar height = eigenvalue magnitude。展示 confounding 的 spectral concentration vs collider 的 dispersion。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Diagnostic heatmap — 对 K=5 confounding DAG，将 C 的 20 维参数空间降至 2D (PCA)，color = bias magnitude。展示 bias landscape 的可视化工具原型。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档下，K=5,7 的 interpretability tools 对 confounding/mediation 有效但对 collider 不足。\n      这意味着论文中 \"eigendecomposition as interpretability tool\" 的 claim 需要加 caveat：\n      仅对 bias 有清晰方向结构的拓扑有效。Worst-case bounds 的 3x conservativeness\n      使其实用价值有限——bound 告诉你 \"bias 最多这么大\" 但实际远小于此。\n      建议：对 collider/M-bias 拓扑放弃 eigendecomposition 摘要，改用 worst-case bound +\n      diagnostic visualization 的组合。论文中坦诚分拓扑讨论可解释性工具的适用范围。\n\n  - name: \"Empirical confusion matrices (3 LLMs × 3 CSS tasks)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: |\n      收集 Llama 4 Maverick / Qwen 3.5 Plus / DeepSeek V4 在 protest event coding (K=5),\n      stance detection (K=3), toxicity (K=2) 上的经验混淆矩阵，分析 inter-model 相关性\n      和 downstream regression bias。\n    expected_results:\n      protest_accuracy_range: \"0.68–0.73\"\n      protest_diagonal_dominance_range: \"0.74–0.80\"\n      stance_accuracy_range: \"0.76–0.81\"\n      stance_diagonal_dominance_range: \"0.82–0.87\"\n      toxicity_accuracy_range: \"0.83–0.88\"\n      inter_model_error_kappa: \"0.58–0.67\"\n      near_permutation_structures_observed: 0\n      downstream_bias_gt_005_count: \"2–3 out of 9\"\n      downstream_direction_reversal_observed: false\n      max_downstream_bias: 0.12\n      total_annotations: \"~270K (30K × 3 models × 3 tasks)\"\n      api_cost_actual: \"$350–480\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      当前 SOTA LLMs 在 well-studied CSS tasks 上准确率 0.68-0.88，产出的混淆矩阵\n      必然 diagonal-dominant。Off-diagonal mass 集中在语义相邻类别（如 stance detection 中\n      \"support\" 与 \"somewhat support\" 互混），而非随机分散——这意味着 C 结构远离\n      near-permutation 极端。Inter-model error kappa 0.58-0.67 与 Kim et al. (ICML 2025)\n      的 60% error agreement 一致，因为 LLM 的错误模式受 pre-training data distribution\n      驱动，不同模型在相同 \"难\" 样本上犯相似错误。Downstream bias 多数 <0.05 因为\n      diagonal-dominant C 的 bias 表达式给出小值；2-3 个 >0.05 的案例出现在 protest event\n      coding（K=5，准确率最低）与较弱模型（Qwen 3.5 Plus）的组合。无方向反转因为：\n      (a) 经验 C 是 diagonal-dominant，远未到 near-permutation threshold，\n      (b) 如果实验设计中 annotated variable 是 confounder/mediator（非 exposure），\n      则即使 C 极端也不会反转（worst 档核心假设）。\n      这是 worst 档最关键的弱点：经验数据 \"太好了\"，极端 C 结构罕见，\n      ASV 和 bias taxonomy 的实用展示受限。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Empirical Confusion Matrices — 9 Combinations\"\n        description: |\n          9 个混淆矩阵（3 LLMs × 3 tasks），每个附 accuracy, diagonal_dominance_ratio,\n          Frobenius_distance_to_identity. Protest K=5 的矩阵最 \"丰富\"（off-diagonal 分散），\n          toxicity K=2 的矩阵最 diagonal-dominant。\n      - name: \"Table 6: Inter-Model Error Correlation\"\n        description: |\n          3×3 模型对的 error agreement matrix（pairwise kappa on error cells）。\n          值 0.58-0.67，证实跨模型错误高度相关。附 per-category breakdown。\n      - name: \"Table 7: Downstream Regression Bias vs Gold Standard\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows × columns: task, model, DAG_topology_assumed, effect_gold, effect_annotated,\n          bias, bias_direction, theoretical_prediction, match (✓/✗).\n          2-3 行 bias >0.05，其余 <0.05。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 9-panel 混淆矩阵 heatmap grid (3 models × 3 tasks)。Color intensity = cell probability。视觉上全部 diagonal-dominant，off-diagonal 仅在 protest K=5 panel 较显著。\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Inter-model error Venn diagram — 展示 3 模型在 stance detection 上的 error overlap。~60% 三模型共同犯错的样本，呼应 Kim et al. 发现。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档的关键困境：经验混淆矩阵全部 diagonal-dominant，无 near-permutation 结构。\n      这意味着：(1) bias taxonomy 的 \"dramatic\" 案例（direction reversal）在实证中不出现，\n      (2) ASV 多数输出 \"robust\"（大 ASV 值），区分力有限，(3) correction guidance 在多数场景\n      退化为 \"MLA suffices\"。应对策略：(a) semi-synthetic 实验——在经验 C 基础上注入\n      controlled perturbation，展示 \"如果 LLM 准确率再低 10% 会怎样\"，\n      (b) 将 diagonal-dominant 本身作为 positive finding（\"当前 LLM 的错误模式在多数 CSS\n      tasks 上落在 safe zone——但 ASV 量化了 safe zone 的边界\"），\n      (c) 增加 4th/5th task（低资源语言 stance detection 或 fine-grained emotion K=7）\n      以提高观察到 non-diagonal-dominant C 的概率。\n\n  - name: \"Binarization collapse analysis (K→2 across 6 topologies)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: |\n      对 6 个拓扑的 K=3,5,7 变量做 binary collapse，比较 full multi-class bias expression\n      与 binarized bias expression 的差异，证明 binarization 不是安全捷径。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_K3_max_delta: 0.078\n      confounding_K5_max_delta: 0.085\n      confounding_K7_max_delta: 0.091\n      exposure_K3_max_delta: 0.072\n      mediation_K3_max_delta: 0.041\n      collider_K3_max_delta: 0.068\n      mbias_K3_max_delta: 0.055\n      instrument_K3_max_delta: 0.038\n      frontdoor_K3_max_delta: 0.045\n      overall_max_delta: 0.091\n      topologies_with_delta_gt_005: 4\n      topologies_with_delta_gt_008: 2\n      binarization_can_reverse_direction: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      Binarization 将 K-class variable collapse 为 binary，丢弃类别间的 fine-grained\n      误分类信息。在 worst 档下，max delta 0.091 低于 MVP 的 0.103（MVP 的 0.103\n      来自特定 near-permutation C 结构 + confounding DAG 的最优案例）。系统搜索发现\n      confounding DAG 仍是 binarization effect 最大的拓扑（residual confounding 对\n      class-collapse 最敏感），而 mediation/instrument 的 delta 较小（<0.05）因为这些拓扑中\n      annotated variable 的 misclassification 本身效应就小，binarization 损失的信息量有限。\n      关键限制：binarization 在 worst 档下未导致方向反转（仅改变 magnitude），\n      削弱了 \"binarization is hazardous\" 的 claim 力度。Delta 0.091 在统计上显著\n      但实质意义存疑——reviewer 可能质疑 \"0.09 的额外 bias 在社会科学效应量通常 0.1-0.3\n      的语境下是否 material\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Binarization Delta — 6 Topologies × K=3,5,7\"\n        description: |\n          ~18 rows (6 topologies × 3 K values) × columns: topology, K, folding_scheme,\n          bias_multiclass, bias_binary, delta, delta/bias_multiclass (relative),\n          direction_change (all \"No\"). Max delta bolded. Confounding rows consistently\n          highest delta.\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Grouped bar chart — x = topology, grouped bars = K=3/5/7, y = |Δ|。 Horizontal line at Δ=0.05 作为 'material threshold'。展示 4/18 bars 超过 threshold。\"\n      - \"Fig 9: Scatter — multi-class bias (x) vs binary bias (y) per configuration, 45° reference line。 Points below line = binarization underestimates bias。展示系统性偏离但 magnitude 有限。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档下 binarization 分析的结论是 \"real but modest\"。Max Δ=0.091 支持\n      \"binary 框架不足\" 的 claim，但不够 dramatic 作为 standalone finding。在 Version B\n      framing 中，binarization 分析应作为 supporting evidence 而非 lead result——\n      它回答的问题从 \"binarization is dangerous\" 降级为 \"binarization loses information\n      that matters for magnitude estimation\"。建议：在论文中将 binarization 分析压缩为\n      1 段 + 1 figure，将篇幅让给 exposure 反转机制的 spectral 分析和 correction framework。\n\n  - name: \"ASV formal proofs (confounding, mediation, collider)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: |\n      为 3 个优先拓扑推导 ASV 表达式，证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness，\n      MC 验证 coverage（90%, 95%, 99%）。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_monotonicity: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      confounding_sharpness: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      confounding_coverage_90: 0.88\n      confounding_coverage_95: 0.93\n      confounding_coverage_99: 0.97\n      mediation_monotonicity: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      mediation_sharpness: \"FAILED — bound conservative by factor 1.4–1.8x\"\n      mediation_coverage_90: 0.86\n      mediation_coverage_95: 0.91\n      mediation_coverage_99: 0.96\n      collider_monotonicity: \"FAILED — 7% of C structures show non-monotone ASV in δ\"\n      collider_sharpness: \"N/A (requires monotonicity)\"\n      collider_coverage_90: 0.74\n      collider_coverage_95: 0.78\n      collider_coverage_99: 0.85\n      asv_sharpness_formal_proofs: 1\n      collider_monotonicity_violation_delta_range: \"0.3–0.5\"\n      collider_violation_C_characterization: \"off-diagonal mass concentrated in 2 adjacent cells\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Confounding ASV monotonicity 成立因为 residual confounding 是 δ 的单调函数——\n      更大的 annotation error amplification 只能增加残差混淆，不能减少。Sharpness 成立因为\n      near-permutation C 结构确实实现了 bound（近似完全 label swap 达到最大 residual confounding）。\n\n      Mediation ASV monotonicity 成立因为 indirect effect 的 attenuation 随 mediator\n      misclassification 单调增加。但 sharpness 失败因为 mediation bias 的 maximum 受限于\n      direct effect magnitude——即使 C 完全 permutation，bias 也不能超过 direct effect，\n      而 ASV bound 的推导假设 bias 可以达到 \"worst-case over all C in δ-ball\"，\n      其中包含了结构上不可达的 C 配置。Bound conservative 1.4-1.8x。\n\n      Collider ASV 是 worst 档的关键难点。Collider bias 来自 conditioning on a common effect——\n      当 collider variable 被 misclassify 时，conditioning 的 \"打开\" 程度取决于 C 结构。\n      在某些 C 结构下（off-diagonal mass 集中在 2 个相邻 cell），δ 从 0.3 增到 0.5 时\n      bias 先增后减——因为中等 misclassification 部分打开 collider path 但保留 conditioning\n      结构，而更大的 misclassification 反而 \"破坏\" 了 conditioning 的精确性，使 collider path\n      的打开效果被噪声稀释。这产生 non-monotone ASV，7% violation rate。\n      修补方案：restricted ASV（限制 δ-path 在 monotone region）或 conditional ASV\n      （对 C 结构分区域定义）。两种方案都增加框架复杂度，降低实用性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: ASV Proof Status Summary\"\n        description: |\n          3 rows (topologies) × columns: monotonicity (✓/✗ + proof type),\n          sharpness (✓/✗ + proof type), coverage_90/95/99, notes.\n          Confounding 行全绿，mediation 行部分黄（sharpness ✗），collider 行红（monotonicity ✗）。\n      - name: \"Table 10: ASV Coverage — 1000 Scenario MC Validation\"\n        description: |\n          详细 coverage 分析。Per topology 的 coverage 分布（不是单个数字）——\n          histogram of \"actual coverage across 1000 scenarios\"。Confounding 集中在 0.92-0.95，\n          collider 分散在 0.65-0.90 with a tail of under-coverage。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: ASV monotonicity diagnostic — 3 panels (topologies)。每 panel 画 ASV(δ) curve for 20 randomly sampled C structures。Confounding/mediation: all curves monotonically increasing。Collider: 2-3 curves show a 'bump' (local maximum) at δ≈0.35，demonstrating non-monotonicity。\"\n      - \"Fig 11: Coverage calibration plot — nominal coverage (x, 0.80-0.99) vs empirical coverage (y)。45° line = perfect calibration。Confounding 紧贴 45° 线，collider 系统性低于 45° 线。\"\n    analysis: |\n      ASV 框架在 worst 档下遭遇了预期中的 collider 难题。Sharpness 仅 1 个拓扑完成证明，\n      低于理想但在 [1,2] 范围内。Collider 的 non-monotonicity 是论文的潜在 weakness——\n      reviewer 会问 \"如果 ASV 在 collider 拓扑不 monotone，你的框架怎么用？\"\n      应对：(1) 论文中诚实报告 collider 的限制，提出 restricted ASV 定义，\n      (2) 强调 collider 在 CSS 实证中相对少见（mediation/confounding 更常见），\n      (3) 将 collider ASV 修复标记为 \"important future work\" 而非尝试勉强证明。\n      Coverage 0.85 (aggregated) 在 [0.80, 0.88] 范围内——不是灾难性的 under-coverage，\n      但需要在论文中解释为什么 coverage 低于 nominal 并建议 practitioners 使用 99% level\n      而非 95% level 作为 conservative 选择。\n\n  - name: \"ASV MC validation (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: |\n      对剩余 3 个拓扑推导 ASV 表达式并做 MC 验证。\n      Monotonicity 和 sharpness 作为 conjecture + numerical evidence，不要求 formal proof。\n    expected_results:\n      mbias_monotonicity_mc: \"holds (0/1000 violations)\"\n      mbias_sharpness_mc: \"not achieved — bound conservative by 1.6–2.1x\"\n      mbias_coverage_95: 0.86\n      instrument_monotonicity_mc: \"holds (0/1000 violations)\"\n      instrument_sharpness_mc: \"near-sharp — within 1.1x in 3% of scenarios\"\n      instrument_coverage_95: 0.88\n      frontdoor_monotonicity_mc: \"holds for 97% of scenarios (3% violations at extreme C)\"\n      frontdoor_sharpness_mc: \"not achieved — bound conservative by 1.8–2.4x\"\n      frontdoor_coverage_95: 0.76\n      aggregate_coverage_95_all_6: 0.85\n    result_rationale: |\n      M-bias 的 monotonicity 成立因为 M-bias 的 bias 结构本质上是两条 confounding path 的\n      叠加——每条 path 的 bias 对 δ 单调，叠加后仍单调。但 sharpness 不成立因为\n      两条 path 的 maximum bias 不能同时达到——worst-case C 对 path 1 最优时，\n      对 path 2 不一定最优，dual-confounder 结构限制了 joint worst case 的可达性。\n\n      Instrument 的 monotonicity 成立因为 IV estimation 的 bias 在 instrument misclassification\n      下是线性的——Wald estimator 的分母（first-stage coefficient）被 attenuation，\n      bias = true_effect × (1 - attenuation_factor)，monotone in δ。Near-sharp 因为\n      IV 的 linear structure 使 bound 很接近 achievable maximum。\n\n      Front-door 有 3% violations 因为 front-door criterion 涉及两步：(1) exposure → mediator\n      和 (2) mediator → outcome（调整 exposure）。在极端 C 下（near-rank-deficient），\n      步骤 (2) 的调整不稳定——small δ change 可能 flip 步骤 (2) 的调整方向，\n      导致总 bias 的 local non-monotonicity。这是 compound estimation 的固有问题，\n      与 collider 的 non-monotonicity 机制不同（collider 是 conditioning 问题，front-door 是\n      调整稳定性问题）。\n\n      Aggregate coverage 0.85：front-door 的 0.76 拉低整体。如果排除 front-door，\n      remaining 5 topologies 的 mean coverage 是 0.87。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: ASV Validation Summary — Remaining 3 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          3 rows × columns: topology, monotonicity_status, violation_rate,\n          sharpness_status, bound_tightness, coverage_90/95/99.\n          附注释解释 front-door 3% violations 的机制。\n      - name: \"Table 12: Aggregate ASV Framework Status — All 6 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          综合 Table 9 和 Table 11 的 summary view。6 rows，每行标注\n          proof_type (formal / MC-conjecture) 和 overall_status (full / partial / needs-repair)。\n          Color-coded: confounding=green, mediation/instrument/mbias=yellow,\n          collider/frontdoor=orange。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: ASV(δ) curves for M-bias/instrument/front-door，与 Fig 10 对应。Instrument curves 最 clean（几乎线性），front-door 有 2-3 条 curves 在极端 C 下出现微弱 non-monotonicity。\"\n    analysis: |\n      5/6 拓扑 monotonicity 基本成立（collider 7% violations + front-door 3% violations\n      是仅有的例外）。从论文叙事角度，这支持 \"ASV 框架在大多数实用场景下有效\" 的 claim，\n      但 \"大多数\" 而非 \"所有\" 是 worst 档的定义性特征。Sharpness 普遍不足——\n      6 个拓扑中仅 confounding 达到 formal sharpness，instrument 接近。\n      这意味着 ASV 在实践中偏 conservative（报告的 robustness 比实际更悲观），\n      对 practitioners 来说是 safe 的方向但削弱了 ASV 的 \"precision\" selling point。\n      Version B framing 将 ASV 定位为 \"magnitude uncertainty 的 robustness measure\"\n      而非 \"direction reversal 的 guard\"——这个定位与 sharpness 不足是兼容的\n      （magnitude uncertainty 不需要 tight bound，conservative 即可）。\n\n  - name: \"ASV empirical calibration (3 tasks × 3 LLMs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: |\n      将 ASV 应用到 plan_003 的经验混淆矩阵，在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage，\n      报告 ASV alongside downstream effect estimates。\n    expected_results:\n      meaningful_asv_count: 4\n      vacuous_asv_count: 5\n      concordance_meaningful: \"4/4 (all meaningful ASVs correctly classify robust vs fragile)\"\n      concordance_total: \"4/9 (5 vacuous cases are trivially correct but uninformative)\"\n      empirical_asv_concordance: 4\n      asv_infinite_or_very_large_cases: 5\n      protest_Qwen_asv: \"finite, ASV=2.3 (fragile)\"\n      protest_Llama_asv: \"finite, ASV=4.1 (moderate)\"\n      stance_DeepSeek_asv: \"large, ASV=18.7 (robust)\"\n      toxicity_all_asv: \">50 (robust, binary special case)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      经验混淆矩阵 diagonal-dominant（plan_003 结果），因此达到 direction-reversing 或\n      magnitude-significant 的 δ threshold 很高——ASV 值大（甚至无穷）。\n      5/9 combinations 的 ASV ≫10，意味着 \"需要当前 annotation error 放大 10 倍以上\n      才会产生有意义的 bias\"——technically correct 但 uninformative（研究者已经知道\n      高准确率 LLM 产生的 bias 小）。4/9 meaningful cases 出现在 K=5 protest event coding\n      （准确率最低，off-diagonal mass 最大）和 K=3 stance detection 与较弱模型的组合。\n      这些 meaningful cases 中 ASV 正确区分了 fragile（ASV<5）vs robust（ASV>10）——\n      但样本量太小（4 cases）无法做统计检验。\n\n      Worst 档的核心困境在此体现：ASV 的理论价值依赖于经验 C 足够 \"interesting\"，\n      但 SOTA LLMs 太好了，经验 C 太 \"boring\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: ASV Values — 9 Combinations\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows × columns: task, model, K, accuracy, diagonal_dominance,\n          ASV_value, ASV_classification (fragile/moderate/robust),\n          held_out_bias, held_out_direction, concordance (✓/✗/trivial).\n          5 行标注 \"trivial\" (ASV>50)，4 行标注 ✓。\n      - name: \"Table 14: ASV vs Raw Confusion Matrix — Interpretability Comparison\"\n        description: |\n          对 4 个 meaningful cases，并排展示 ASV summary 和 raw confusion matrix，\n          说明 ASV 提供了哪些 confusion matrix 本身不直接给出的信息\n          （主要是 \"离 danger zone 有多远\" 的距离度量）。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 13: ASV sensitivity curve — 对 protest/Qwen (ASV=2.3) case，画 bias magnitude as function of δ amplification factor。Vertical line at δ=1 (current error)，δ=2.3 处 bias crosses significance threshold。展示 ASV 的可视化解读。\"\n      - \"Fig 14: ASV distribution across 9 combinations — dot plot with log scale y axis。Clear separation between 4 finite-meaningful (ASV 2-5) and 5 vacuous (ASV >15) cases。\"\n    analysis: |\n      4/9 concordance 在 [3,6] 范围的低端。论文叙事需要将这个结果 reframe：\n      不是 \"ASV 在 9 个场景中只有 4 个有用\"，而是 \"ASV 正确识别了 4 个值得关注的\n      high-risk combinations——这些是研究者在没有 ASV 的情况下可能忽略的\"。\n      对 5 个 vacuous cases，论文可以说 \"ASV 为这些 combinations 提供了 formal robustness\n      guarantee，研究者可以安心使用\"——但 reviewer 可能反驳 \"any reasonable researcher\n      wouldn't worry about a 85%-accurate annotator\"。\n\n      增强策略：(a) semi-synthetic 注入——在经验 C 上添加 controlled degradation\n      （accuracy 从 0.8 降至 0.5），展示 ASV 如何从 \"robust\" 转变为 \"fragile\"，\n      (b) 增加低资源任务（如小语种情感分析 K=7），提高观察到 meaningful ASV 的概率，\n      (c) user study——给研究者展示 ASV vs 不展示 ASV，测量决策质量差异。\n\n  - name: \"Correction guidance framework\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: |\n      构建 {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction method 的决策框架，\n      MC 验证 recommended method 在 ≥90% scenarios 产生最小 bias，\n      经验数据验证。\n    expected_results:\n      overall_accuracy: 0.78\n      mla_recommendation_fraction: 0.65\n      exposure_reversal_recommendation: \"gold label collection / no adequate correction\"\n      exposure_accuracy: 0.85\n      confounding_accuracy: 0.82\n      collider_accuracy: 0.68\n      scenarios_where_no_method_adequate: 0.12\n      ppi_outperforms_mla_fraction: 0.08\n      dsl_applicable_fraction: 0.05\n      naive_plugin_never_recommended: true\n      correction_framework_accuracy: 0.78\n      decision_tree_depth: 4\n      decision_tree_leaf_purity: 0.73\n    result_rationale: |\n      Correction framework accuracy 0.78 反映了 worst 档的核心预测：framework 在多数场景\n      退化为 \"use MLA\"。当 65% 的 scenarios 的最优推荐是 MLA 时，一个 trivial baseline\n      \"always recommend MLA\" 就有 65% accuracy——framework 的 0.78 仅比 trivial baseline\n      高 13 个百分点，discriminative value 有限。\n\n      MLA 主导的原因：MLA (Measurement-error Likelihood Adjustment) 是最 general 的方法，\n      它利用 C 矩阵估计对 likelihood 做调整，适用于任何 topology + 任何 error structure。\n      在 5 个 \"well-behaved\" topology（方向可预测）中，MLA 几乎总是最优选择因为它直接\n      纠正 bias magnitude。PPI 仅在 finite-sample regime（small gold sample + large LLM sample）\n      优于 MLA（8% scenarios）。DSL 仅在 very specific conditions（已知 C + linear model）下\n      优于 MLA（5% scenarios）。\n\n      Exposure topology 是 framework 最有价值的部分——对 reversal-risk scenarios，framework\n      正确推荐 \"no correction adequate without gold labels\"，这是 non-trivial guidance\n      （naive researcher 可能尝试 MLA 但 MLA 在 sign-reversed regime 可能 amplify error）。\n\n      Collider accuracy 最低（0.68）因为 collider bias correction 依赖于 conditioning strategy——\n      \"correct the annotation then re-condition\" vs \"don't condition at all\" 的选择\n      取决于 effect magnitude 和 C structure 的交互，decision tree 难以准确捕获。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Correction Guidance Decision Framework\"\n        description: |\n          Matrix format: rows = topologies (6), columns = error structure categories\n          (diagonal-dominant / moderate / near-permutation × differential / non-differential),\n          cells = recommended method + ASV threshold. 大量 cells 填入 \"MLA\"。\n          Exposure 行的 near-permutation cells 标红 \"gold labels required\"。\n      - name: \"Table 16: Framework Accuracy — MC Validation\"\n        description: |\n          Per topology accuracy, per error-structure accuracy, confusion matrix of\n          {recommended method × actually-best method}. 最大 off-diagonal cluster:\n          MLA recommended but PPI actually marginally better (差异 <0.01 bias)。\n      - name: \"Table 17: Open Problem Identification\"\n        description: |\n          12% of scenarios 标记为 \"no existing method adequate\"。\n          Columns: scenario_description, why_inadequate, required_capability.\n          主要集中在 differential multi-class error + complex topology (M-bias, front-door)\n          和 correlated multi-LLM error。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 15: Decision tree visualization — depth 4, 12 leaves。Color = recommended method。大量绿色叶节点（MLA），少量红色（gold labels）和蓝色（PPI）。视觉上展示 'MLA 主导' 的现实。\"\n      - \"Fig 16: Framework accuracy vs ASV — scatter plot，x = ASV magnitude，y = framework recommendation correct (1/0)。低 ASV（fragile）区域 accuracy 更高（framework 更有价值），高 ASV（robust）区域 accuracy 无意义（任何推荐都 work）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Correction framework 在 worst 档下的 selling point 不是 accuracy 而是 completeness——\n      \"first systematic mapping of when each correction method applies, with identified open problems\"。\n      0.78 accuracy 加上 MLA 65% dominance 意味着 framework 的 practical value 集中在\n      ~35% non-MLA scenarios（exposure reversal + PPI edge cases + no-method-adequate regimes）。\n      Version B narrative 中 Claim 3 权重增加，需要将 framework 包装为 \"practitioner's guide\"\n      而非 \"automated decision system\"——降低 accuracy 期望，强调 \"the framework identifies\n      what you should worry about, not just what to do\"。\n      Open problems 部分（12% no-method-adequate）可能是最有 citation value 的贡献——\n      明确指出 correlated multi-LLM error correction 是 unsolved problem，引导后续研究。\n\n  - name: \"Pathological confusion matrix analysis (spectral)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: |\n      分析极端 C 结构（near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal）在 6 个拓扑下的\n      bias 行为，用 spectral 分析（eigenvalue spectrum of C）识别 bias severity 的\n      structural predictors。\n    expected_results:\n      exposure_reversal_spectral_threshold: \"λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 for K=3\"\n      exposure_reversal_prediction_auc: 0.92\n      diagonal_dominance_as_simple_predictor: \"reversal when diag_dom < 0.45\"\n      diagonal_dominance_prediction_auc: 0.89\n      other_topologies_spectral_finding: \"monotone relationship between λ₁ and bias magnitude; no reversal threshold exists\"\n      spectral_gap_predicts_magnitude_R2: 0.78\n      block_diagonal_C_magnitude_effect: \"1.5–2.3x bias amplification vs random C of same accuracy\"\n      rank_deficient_C_behavior: \"bias expressions numerically unstable, need regularization\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Exposure DAG 的反转机制有清晰的 spectral interpretation：C 矩阵的 eigendecomposition\n      中，λ₁ 对应 \"correct classification\" mode（沿 identity 方向），λ₂ 对应 \"dominant confusion\"\n      mode（label swap 方向）。当 λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 时，confusion mode 足够强以翻转 treatment\n      assignment 的有效方向，产生 sign reversal。这个阈值在 K=3 下给出 AUC 0.92 的\n      reversal 预测——spectral gap 是一个 principled predictor。\n      Diagonal dominance（diag_dom = min_i C_ii / max_i Σ_{j≠i} C_ij）是更简单的 proxy，\n      AUC 0.89 略低但更直观。\n\n      对其余 5 个拓扑，spectral 分析揭示 λ₁ 与 bias magnitude 的 monotone relationship\n      （R²=0.78），但没有 \"reversal threshold\"——bias 方向由 topology 的结构性质决定\n      （confounding → toward OVB, mediation → toward attenuation, etc.），C 的 spectrum\n      只调制 magnitude。这在理论上不意外（worst 档假设），但提供了一个\n      compact characterization。\n\n      Block-diagonal C（如 K=6 分成两个 K=3 block，block 间无混淆）产生 1.5-2.3x\n      bias amplification 因为 block 结构创造了 \"structured confusion\"——模型在 block 内\n      混淆但 block 间清晰，这比同等 accuracy 的 random C 产生更大 bias\n      因为 confusion 集中而非分散。\n\n      Rank-deficient C 导致某些 bias 表达式的矩阵求逆不稳定——这是实际计算中的\n      nuisance，不是理论 insight，但需要在 toolkit 中处理（regularization）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 18: Spectral Predictors of Bias Severity\"\n        description: |\n          Columns: predictor (λ₂/λ₁, diag_dom, spectral_gap, Frobenius_norm),\n          target (reversal_binary, bias_magnitude), topology, AUC_or_R².\n          Exposure rows 有 reversal prediction AUC，其余行仅有 magnitude R²。\n      - name: \"Table 19: Pathological C Structure Catalog\"\n        description: |\n          Catalog of 4 pathological C types × 6 topologies × {bias_magnitude,\n          direction_preserved, numerical_stability}。27 行 summary。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 17: Spectral gap vs bias — 2 panels。Left: exposure DAG，scatter with reversal colored red/blue，clear threshold at λ₂/λ₁=0.6。Right: confounding DAG，smooth monotone curve，no threshold。最直观的 'dichotomy' spectral evidence。\"\n      - \"Fig 18: Block-diagonal C amplification — bar chart comparing bias from block-diagonal vs random C at matched accuracy, across 6 topologies。展示 structured confusion 的 amplification effect。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Spectral 分析在 worst 档下提供了 exposure 反转的 mechanistic explanation——\n      这是 narrative 需要的 \"deep dive\"。λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 threshold 是一个 actionable\n      practitioner guideline（\"检查你的 confusion matrix 的 spectral gap，如果 < 0.4\n      则 exposure 标注安全\"）。对其余拓扑，spectral 分析的贡献更 modest——\n      确认了 \"方向可预测，magnitude 依赖 C\" 的结论但没有 surprising insight。\n      Block-diagonal 发现是 bonus 内容——在 CSS 中，block-diagonal C 对应\n      \"模型区分粗粒度类别但混淆细粒度类别\" 的常见模式，有实际意义。\n      建议在论文中将 spectral 分析作为 Section 4 的 highlight（exposure deep dive），\n      其余拓扑的 spectral 结果放 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"annot-sensitivity Python toolkit\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: |\n      Open-source Python 包：用户输入 DAG + confusion matrix + downstream estimate →\n      输出 bias expressions + ASV bounds + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation\n      + diagnostic plots。pip-installable，每个 topology 一个 worked example。\n    expected_results:\n      pip_installable: true\n      supported_topologies: 6\n      K_range_supported: \"2–15\"\n      runtime_K3: \"<0.1s\"\n      runtime_K7: \"<1s\"\n      runtime_K15: \"<10s\"\n      worked_examples: 6\n      api_surface: \"BiasExpr, ASV, CorrectionGuide, DiagnosticPlot\"\n      test_coverage: \"~85%\"\n      documentation_pages: \"~20\"\n      demo_value_assessment: \"limited by diagonal-dominant empirical C\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Toolkit 是 engineering deliverable 而非实验。在 worst 档下，toolkit 本身功能完整\n      但 demonstration value 受限：经验混淆矩阵太 diagonal-dominant，toolkit 在 demo 中\n      主要输出 \"your annotation is fine\"——不够 compelling 作为 conference demo。\n      Worked examples 需要用 semi-synthetic C 而非 pure empirical C 来展示\n      toolkit 的 full capability（包括 reversal detection, ASV fragility warning, etc.）。\n      Runtime 快（K≤7 < 1s）因为 bias expressions 是 closed-form matrix operations，\n      不需要 MC simulation。K=15 需要 ~10s 因为 15×15 矩阵的 eigendecomposition\n      和 worst-case optimization 增加计算量。\n      作为 Claim 3 (\"correction guidance\") 的 tangible artifact，toolkit 增加论文的\n      practical impact——即使理论贡献在 worst 档下被削弱，一个 pip-installable tool\n      是 reviewer 认可的 concrete contribution。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 19: Toolkit workflow diagram — input (DAG graph + C matrix + β̂) → 4 outputs (bias expression + ASV + sensitivity curve + correction recommendation)。展示 API 的 end-to-end flow。\"\n      - \"Fig 20: Toolkit screenshot — 对 protest/Qwen case (ASV=2.3) 的实际输出截图，包括 sensitivity curve plot 和 correction recommendation。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Toolkit 在 worst 档下是 \"保底贡献\"——即使 taxonomy 不够 dramatic、ASV 有 coverage 问题、\n      correction framework 主要推荐 MLA，一个 well-documented open-source tool 仍有独立价值。\n      建议在论文中给 toolkit 一个 dedicated subsection（不只是 \"code available at github\"），\n      展示 API 设计和 worked examples。在 supplementary material 中包含\n      comprehensive tutorial notebook。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10917,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10917},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd93169f-899b-425b-835b-3968c6801b13","uuid":"301f8bf0-ed26-4c4b-a2a8-91a0329230a0"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":542847,"duration_api_ms":544317,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Version B framing. Lead finding: \"multi-class annotation error 的危险性是 topology-dependent 的：\n  exposure misclassification 在方向和幅度上均不可预测，其余拓扑方向可预测但幅度需全 K×K 矩阵\n  才能量化——binary 框架在两种情况下均不足。\" Claim 1 从 \"breaks guarantees across topologies\"\n  调整为 \"reveals a sharp topology-dependent dichotomy\"——exposure 是唯一方向不可预测的拓扑，\n  这本身是重要发现（exposure 是 CSS 中最常被 LLM 标注的变量）。Claim 2 的 ASV 从\n  \"robustness to direction reversal\" 调整为 \"robustness to magnitude uncertainty\"，\n  因 collider ASV 单调性部分失效（7% violations），需修改定义或加条件，降低紧性要求。\n  Claim 3 权重增加——correction guidance 的实用价值成为主要卖点，弥补 taxonomy 发现不够 dramatic。\n  需额外投入：(a) spectral 分析深挖 exposure 反转机制（λ₂/λ₁ 阈值），\n  (b) 经验实验扩充至 4-5 个 task 以补偿理论贡献缩窄，\n  (c) 考虑 user study 展示 ASV 对研究者决策的影响。\n  theory-MC match 在复杂拓扑（front-door, collider）偏低，需坦诚承认闭合形式表达式的近似局限性，\n  将 MC 验证本身作为补充贡献。经验混淆矩阵 diagonal-dominant，极端 C 结构罕见——\n  ASV 在多数实证场景输出 \"robust\"，实用区分力有限，需通过 semi-synthetic 注入实验补救。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Six-topology bias taxonomy (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: |\n      对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）\n      推导 K=3 闭合形式 bias 表达式，用 MC 验证（1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 种 C 结构）。\n      核心问题：哪些拓扑在 non-differential K≥3 误分类下出现方向反转？\n    expected_results:\n      reversal_topologies_count: 1\n      confounding_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      confounding_theory_mc_match: \"6/6\"\n      confounding_bias_range: \"0.063–0.298\"\n      exposure_reversal_rate: 0.85\n      exposure_sign_reversal_rate: 0.834\n      exposure_amplification_rate: 0.141\n      exposure_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      exposure_bias_range: \"-0.84–0.42\"\n      mediation_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      mediation_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      mediation_bias_range: \"0.00–0.15\"\n      collider_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      collider_theory_mc_match: \"4/6\"\n      collider_bias_range: \"0.02–0.18\"\n      mbias_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      mbias_theory_mc_match: \"4/6\"\n      mbias_bias_range: \"0.04–0.22\"\n      instrument_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      instrument_theory_mc_match: \"5/6\"\n      instrument_bias_range: \"0.03–0.25\"\n      frontdoor_reversal_rate: 0.0\n      frontdoor_theory_mc_match: \"3/6\"\n      frontdoor_bias_range: \"0.01–0.19\"\n      overall_theory_mc_match: \"32/42 (0.76)\"\n      random_100k_reversal_topologies: \"exposure only\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst 档的核心预测：仅 exposure DAG 出现方向反转。机制上，exposure misclassification\n      直接扰乱 treatment assignment labels——当 K≥3 时，near-permutation C 导致 label swap，\n      将 treatment A 的 outcome 映射到 treatment B 的估计上，产生符号翻转。这在 K=2 时\n      结构性不可能（binary 只有\"正确/错误\"两种状态，non-differential 保证 bias toward null）。\n      其余 5 个拓扑中，misclassified 变量（confounder/mediator/collider/instrument/front-door variable）\n      不直接定义 treatment contrast，其误分类调制 bias magnitude 但不翻转 numerator/denominator，\n      因此方向可预测。Theory-MC match 率 0.76 偏低的原因：collider（conditioning 引入非线性）、\n      M-bias（双 confounder 路径交互）、front-door（复合 mediation 步骤）的闭合形式表达式\n      在 extreme C structures 下需要高阶 Taylor 项，一阶近似不够精确。Front-door 最差（3/6），\n      因为 front-door criterion 涉及两步 mediation，每步的近似误差在复合后被放大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Six-Topology Bias Taxonomy Summary (K=3)\"\n        description: |\n          6 rows (topologies) × columns: reversal_rate_100k, named_structure_match (x/6),\n          bias_range [min, max], bias_direction_class (monotonic-toward-null / monotonic-toward-OVB /\n          unpredictable), mechanism_summary.\n          Key pattern: exposure 行显著异于其余——reversal 85%，direction unpredictable；\n          其余 5 行 reversal 0%，方向可预测，但 magnitude range 差异大\n          （confounding 0.06-0.30 vs mediation 0.00-0.15 vs collider 0.02-0.18）。\n      - name: \"Table 2: Theory vs MC Bias — Per-Structure Detail\"\n        description: |\n          42 rows (6 topologies × ~7 structures including identity-adjacent, uniform-leaning,\n          near-permutation, block-diagonal, asymmetric, random-moderate, plus MVP-inherited).\n          Columns: topology, C_structure, theoretical_bias, mc_mean, mc_95ci, match (✓/✗).\n          10 个 ✗ 集中在 collider-near-permutation, mbias-block-diagonal,\n          frontdoor-near-permutation/asymmetric/block-diagonal。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Heatmap — topology (y) × C-structure (x)，color = signed bias magnitude。Exposure 行出现蓝红交替（正负 bias），其余行单色渐变（单调）。最直观的 'dichotomy' 可视化。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter — theoretical bias (x) vs MC mean bias (y)，per topology color-coded。理想 y=x 线上 confounding/exposure 点紧贴，front-door 点偏离最大。附 R² per topology。\"\n      - \"Fig 3: 100k random C density plot — per topology 的 bias distribution。Exposure 双峰分布（正负），其余单峰。\"\n    analysis: |\n      核心结论：topology-dependent dichotomy 成立但 dramatic 程度有限。Exposure 是唯一 \"dangerous\"\n      拓扑，其余 5 个是 \"well-behaved\"。这支持 Version B framing，但问题是 5 个 well-behaved\n      拓扑的故事不够 exciting——\"magnitude varies but direction is predictable\" 比\n      \"guarantees break\" 弱得多。Theory-MC mismatch 在复杂拓扑的存在是双刃剑：一方面暴露\n      闭合表达式的局限性（reviewer concern），另一方面 MC 验证本身成为必要贡献\n      （\"我们提供的不仅是理论，还有数值验证\"）。Front-door 3/6 match 可能需要在论文中\n      降格为 \"MC-validated conjecture\" 而非 \"theorem\"。\n      Version B lead: 虽然 5 个拓扑方向可预测，但 magnitude range 的跨拓扑差异\n      （confounding 0.06-0.30 vs mediation 0.00-0.15）本身有信息量——研究者需要知道\n      自己的 DAG topology 处于哪个 magnitude regime，binary 框架无法提供这个信息。\n\n  - name: \"General-K matrix expressions and interpretability (K=5,7)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: |\n      将 bias 表达式推广到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式，开发三个可解释性工具：\n      (a) eigendecomposition 摘要，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\n      在 confounding + mediation + collider 上验证。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.82\n      confounding_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.76\n      mediation_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.75\n      mediation_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.68\n      collider_K5_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.58\n      collider_K7_dominant_eigenvalue_fraction: 0.49\n      K5_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.70\n      K7_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.63\n      worst_case_bound_tightness_K5: \"1.8–2.5x conservative\"\n      worst_case_bound_tightness_K7: \"2.5–3.2x conservative\"\n      modes_needed_for_90pct_variance_collider_K7: 4\n    result_rationale: |\n      K 增大时，C 的自由度从 K=3 的 6 个增长到 K=5 的 20 个、K=7 的 42 个。\n      Confounding DAG 的 bias 有简单的方向结构（residual confounding 沿单一方向累积），\n      因此 dominant eigenvalue 即使在 K=7 仍捕获 76% variance——eigendecomposition 是有效的摘要工具。\n      Collider DAG 的 bias 来自 conditioning 引入的伪相关，其方向依赖于 collider 各类别间的\n      相对误分类强度——K=7 时 7 个类别的两两误分类形成多维度干扰，dominant eigenvalue 仅捕获\n      49%，需要 4 个 mode 才能解释 90% variance，eigendecomposition 失去摘要价值。\n      Worst-case bounds 松的原因：bounds 必须覆盖 adversarial C 结构，但实际 C 的 feasible region\n      在高 K 时是高维空间中的低维 manifold——bounds 优化的 supremum 在实践中不可达。\n      Theory-MC match 在 K=7 降至 0.63，因为矩阵形式表达式中的 Kronecker product 项\n      在数值求解时积累舍入误差，且 MC 的 N=10000 在 K=7 时 per-cell 样本量不足\n      （7×7=49 cells，某些 cell 可能 <50 observations）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Eigendecomposition Summary — K=3,5,7 × 3 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows (3 K × 3 topologies) × columns: K, topology, λ₁/tr(Λ), modes_for_90pct,\n          dominant_mode_interpretation, bound_tightness_ratio.\n          Key pattern: confounding 始终 clean（1-2 modes），collider 随 K 增长迅速恶化。\n      - name: \"Table 4: Worst-Case Scalar Bound vs Actual MC Maximum Bias\"\n        description: |\n          展示 bound 的 conservativeness。Columns: topology, K, worst_case_bound,\n          mc_observed_max, ratio. Ratio 从 K=3 的 1.3x 增长到 K=7 的 3.2x。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Eigenvalue spectrum bar chart — 3 panels (K=3,5,7)，每 panel 3 条 bar groups (topologies)，bar height = eigenvalue magnitude。展示 confounding 的 spectral concentration vs collider 的 dispersion。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Diagnostic heatmap — 对 K=5 confounding DAG，将 C 的 20 维参数空间降至 2D (PCA)，color = bias magnitude。展示 bias landscape 的可视化工具原型。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档下，K=5,7 的 interpretability tools 对 confounding/mediation 有效但对 collider 不足。\n      这意味着论文中 \"eigendecomposition as interpretability tool\" 的 claim 需要加 caveat：\n      仅对 bias 有清晰方向结构的拓扑有效。Worst-case bounds 的 3x conservativeness\n      使其实用价值有限——bound 告诉你 \"bias 最多这么大\" 但实际远小于此。\n      建议：对 collider/M-bias 拓扑放弃 eigendecomposition 摘要，改用 worst-case bound +\n      diagnostic visualization 的组合。论文中坦诚分拓扑讨论可解释性工具的适用范围。\n\n  - name: \"Empirical confusion matrices (3 LLMs × 3 CSS tasks)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: |\n      收集 Llama 4 Maverick / Qwen 3.5 Plus / DeepSeek V4 在 protest event coding (K=5),\n      stance detection (K=3), toxicity (K=2) 上的经验混淆矩阵，分析 inter-model 相关性\n      和 downstream regression bias。\n    expected_results:\n      protest_accuracy_range: \"0.68–0.73\"\n      protest_diagonal_dominance_range: \"0.74–0.80\"\n      stance_accuracy_range: \"0.76–0.81\"\n      stance_diagonal_dominance_range: \"0.82–0.87\"\n      toxicity_accuracy_range: \"0.83–0.88\"\n      inter_model_error_kappa: \"0.58–0.67\"\n      near_permutation_structures_observed: 0\n      downstream_bias_gt_005_count: \"2–3 out of 9\"\n      downstream_direction_reversal_observed: false\n      max_downstream_bias: 0.12\n      total_annotations: \"~270K (30K × 3 models × 3 tasks)\"\n      api_cost_actual: \"$350–480\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      当前 SOTA LLMs 在 well-studied CSS tasks 上准确率 0.68-0.88，产出的混淆矩阵\n      必然 diagonal-dominant。Off-diagonal mass 集中在语义相邻类别（如 stance detection 中\n      \"support\" 与 \"somewhat support\" 互混），而非随机分散——这意味着 C 结构远离\n      near-permutation 极端。Inter-model error kappa 0.58-0.67 与 Kim et al. (ICML 2025)\n      的 60% error agreement 一致，因为 LLM 的错误模式受 pre-training data distribution\n      驱动，不同模型在相同 \"难\" 样本上犯相似错误。Downstream bias 多数 <0.05 因为\n      diagonal-dominant C 的 bias 表达式给出小值；2-3 个 >0.05 的案例出现在 protest event\n      coding（K=5，准确率最低）与较弱模型（Qwen 3.5 Plus）的组合。无方向反转因为：\n      (a) 经验 C 是 diagonal-dominant，远未到 near-permutation threshold，\n      (b) 如果实验设计中 annotated variable 是 confounder/mediator（非 exposure），\n      则即使 C 极端也不会反转（worst 档核心假设）。\n      这是 worst 档最关键的弱点：经验数据 \"太好了\"，极端 C 结构罕见，\n      ASV 和 bias taxonomy 的实用展示受限。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Empirical Confusion Matrices — 9 Combinations\"\n        description: |\n          9 个混淆矩阵（3 LLMs × 3 tasks），每个附 accuracy, diagonal_dominance_ratio,\n          Frobenius_distance_to_identity. Protest K=5 的矩阵最 \"丰富\"（off-diagonal 分散），\n          toxicity K=2 的矩阵最 diagonal-dominant。\n      - name: \"Table 6: Inter-Model Error Correlation\"\n        description: |\n          3×3 模型对的 error agreement matrix（pairwise kappa on error cells）。\n          值 0.58-0.67，证实跨模型错误高度相关。附 per-category breakdown。\n      - name: \"Table 7: Downstream Regression Bias vs Gold Standard\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows × columns: task, model, DAG_topology_assumed, effect_gold, effect_annotated,\n          bias, bias_direction, theoretical_prediction, match (✓/✗).\n          2-3 行 bias >0.05，其余 <0.05。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 9-panel 混淆矩阵 heatmap grid (3 models × 3 tasks)。Color intensity = cell probability。视觉上全部 diagonal-dominant，off-diagonal 仅在 protest K=5 panel 较显著。\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Inter-model error Venn diagram — 展示 3 模型在 stance detection 上的 error overlap。~60% 三模型共同犯错的样本，呼应 Kim et al. 发现。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档的关键困境：经验混淆矩阵全部 diagonal-dominant，无 near-permutation 结构。\n      这意味着：(1) bias taxonomy 的 \"dramatic\" 案例（direction reversal）在实证中不出现，\n      (2) ASV 多数输出 \"robust\"（大 ASV 值），区分力有限，(3) correction guidance 在多数场景\n      退化为 \"MLA suffices\"。应对策略：(a) semi-synthetic 实验——在经验 C 基础上注入\n      controlled perturbation，展示 \"如果 LLM 准确率再低 10% 会怎样\"，\n      (b) 将 diagonal-dominant 本身作为 positive finding（\"当前 LLM 的错误模式在多数 CSS\n      tasks 上落在 safe zone——但 ASV 量化了 safe zone 的边界\"），\n      (c) 增加 4th/5th task（低资源语言 stance detection 或 fine-grained emotion K=7）\n      以提高观察到 non-diagonal-dominant C 的概率。\n\n  - name: \"Binarization collapse analysis (K→2 across 6 topologies)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: |\n      对 6 个拓扑的 K=3,5,7 变量做 binary collapse，比较 full multi-class bias expression\n      与 binarized bias expression 的差异，证明 binarization 不是安全捷径。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_K3_max_delta: 0.078\n      confounding_K5_max_delta: 0.085\n      confounding_K7_max_delta: 0.091\n      exposure_K3_max_delta: 0.072\n      mediation_K3_max_delta: 0.041\n      collider_K3_max_delta: 0.068\n      mbias_K3_max_delta: 0.055\n      instrument_K3_max_delta: 0.038\n      frontdoor_K3_max_delta: 0.045\n      overall_max_delta: 0.091\n      topologies_with_delta_gt_005: 4\n      topologies_with_delta_gt_008: 2\n      binarization_can_reverse_direction: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      Binarization 将 K-class variable collapse 为 binary，丢弃类别间的 fine-grained\n      误分类信息。在 worst 档下，max delta 0.091 低于 MVP 的 0.103（MVP 的 0.103\n      来自特定 near-permutation C 结构 + confounding DAG 的最优案例）。系统搜索发现\n      confounding DAG 仍是 binarization effect 最大的拓扑（residual confounding 对\n      class-collapse 最敏感），而 mediation/instrument 的 delta 较小（<0.05）因为这些拓扑中\n      annotated variable 的 misclassification 本身效应就小，binarization 损失的信息量有限。\n      关键限制：binarization 在 worst 档下未导致方向反转（仅改变 magnitude），\n      削弱了 \"binarization is hazardous\" 的 claim 力度。Delta 0.091 在统计上显著\n      但实质意义存疑——reviewer 可能质疑 \"0.09 的额外 bias 在社会科学效应量通常 0.1-0.3\n      的语境下是否 material\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Binarization Delta — 6 Topologies × K=3,5,7\"\n        description: |\n          ~18 rows (6 topologies × 3 K values) × columns: topology, K, folding_scheme,\n          bias_multiclass, bias_binary, delta, delta/bias_multiclass (relative),\n          direction_change (all \"No\"). Max delta bolded. Confounding rows consistently\n          highest delta.\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Grouped bar chart — x = topology, grouped bars = K=3/5/7, y = |Δ|。 Horizontal line at Δ=0.05 作为 'material threshold'。展示 4/18 bars 超过 threshold。\"\n      - \"Fig 9: Scatter — multi-class bias (x) vs binary bias (y) per configuration, 45° reference line。 Points below line = binarization underestimates bias。展示系统性偏离但 magnitude 有限。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst 档下 binarization 分析的结论是 \"real but modest\"。Max Δ=0.091 支持\n      \"binary 框架不足\" 的 claim，但不够 dramatic 作为 standalone finding。在 Version B\n      framing 中，binarization 分析应作为 supporting evidence 而非 lead result——\n      它回答的问题从 \"binarization is dangerous\" 降级为 \"binarization loses information\n      that matters for magnitude estimation\"。建议：在论文中将 binarization 分析压缩为\n      1 段 + 1 figure，将篇幅让给 exposure 反转机制的 spectral 分析和 correction framework。\n\n  - name: \"ASV formal proofs (confounding, mediation, collider)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: |\n      为 3 个优先拓扑推导 ASV 表达式，证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness，\n      MC 验证 coverage（90%, 95%, 99%）。\n    expected_results:\n      confounding_monotonicity: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      confounding_sharpness: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      confounding_coverage_90: 0.88\n      confounding_coverage_95: 0.93\n      confounding_coverage_99: 0.97\n      mediation_monotonicity: \"PROVED (formal)\"\n      mediation_sharpness: \"FAILED — bound conservative by factor 1.4–1.8x\"\n      mediation_coverage_90: 0.86\n      mediation_coverage_95: 0.91\n      mediation_coverage_99: 0.96\n      collider_monotonicity: \"FAILED — 7% of C structures show non-monotone ASV in δ\"\n      collider_sharpness: \"N/A (requires monotonicity)\"\n      collider_coverage_90: 0.74\n      collider_coverage_95: 0.78\n      collider_coverage_99: 0.85\n      asv_sharpness_formal_proofs: 1\n      collider_monotonicity_violation_delta_range: \"0.3–0.5\"\n      collider_violation_C_characterization: \"off-diagonal mass concentrated in 2 adjacent cells\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Confounding ASV monotonicity 成立因为 residual confounding 是 δ 的单调函数——\n      更大的 annotation error amplification 只能增加残差混淆，不能减少。Sharpness 成立因为\n      near-permutation C 结构确实实现了 bound（近似完全 label swap 达到最大 residual confounding）。\n\n      Mediation ASV monotonicity 成立因为 indirect effect 的 attenuation 随 mediator\n      misclassification 单调增加。但 sharpness 失败因为 mediation bias 的 maximum 受限于\n      direct effect magnitude——即使 C 完全 permutation，bias 也不能超过 direct effect，\n      而 ASV bound 的推导假设 bias 可以达到 \"worst-case over all C in δ-ball\"，\n      其中包含了结构上不可达的 C 配置。Bound conservative 1.4-1.8x。\n\n      Collider ASV 是 worst 档的关键难点。Collider bias 来自 conditioning on a common effect——\n      当 collider variable 被 misclassify 时，conditioning 的 \"打开\" 程度取决于 C 结构。\n      在某些 C 结构下（off-diagonal mass 集中在 2 个相邻 cell），δ 从 0.3 增到 0.5 时\n      bias 先增后减——因为中等 misclassification 部分打开 collider path 但保留 conditioning\n      结构，而更大的 misclassification 反而 \"破坏\" 了 conditioning 的精确性，使 collider path\n      的打开效果被噪声稀释。这产生 non-monotone ASV，7% violation rate。\n      修补方案：restricted ASV（限制 δ-path 在 monotone region）或 conditional ASV\n      （对 C 结构分区域定义）。两种方案都增加框架复杂度，降低实用性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: ASV Proof Status Summary\"\n        description: |\n          3 rows (topologies) × columns: monotonicity (✓/✗ + proof type),\n          sharpness (✓/✗ + proof type), coverage_90/95/99, notes.\n          Confounding 行全绿，mediation 行部分黄（sharpness ✗），collider 行红（monotonicity ✗）。\n      - name: \"Table 10: ASV Coverage — 1000 Scenario MC Validation\"\n        description: |\n          详细 coverage 分析。Per topology 的 coverage 分布（不是单个数字）——\n          histogram of \"actual coverage across 1000 scenarios\"。Confounding 集中在 0.92-0.95，\n          collider 分散在 0.65-0.90 with a tail of under-coverage。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: ASV monotonicity diagnostic — 3 panels (topologies)。每 panel 画 ASV(δ) curve for 20 randomly sampled C structures。Confounding/mediation: all curves monotonically increasing。Collider: 2-3 curves show a 'bump' (local maximum) at δ≈0.35，demonstrating non-monotonicity。\"\n      - \"Fig 11: Coverage calibration plot — nominal coverage (x, 0.80-0.99) vs empirical coverage (y)。45° line = perfect calibration。Confounding 紧贴 45° 线，collider 系统性低于 45° 线。\"\n    analysis: |\n      ASV 框架在 worst 档下遭遇了预期中的 collider 难题。Sharpness 仅 1 个拓扑完成证明，\n      低于理想但在 [1,2] 范围内。Collider 的 non-monotonicity 是论文的潜在 weakness——\n      reviewer 会问 \"如果 ASV 在 collider 拓扑不 monotone，你的框架怎么用？\"\n      应对：(1) 论文中诚实报告 collider 的限制，提出 restricted ASV 定义，\n      (2) 强调 collider 在 CSS 实证中相对少见（mediation/confounding 更常见），\n      (3) 将 collider ASV 修复标记为 \"important future work\" 而非尝试勉强证明。\n      Coverage 0.85 (aggregated) 在 [0.80, 0.88] 范围内——不是灾难性的 under-coverage，\n      但需要在论文中解释为什么 coverage 低于 nominal 并建议 practitioners 使用 99% level\n      而非 95% level 作为 conservative 选择。\n\n  - name: \"ASV MC validation (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: |\n      对剩余 3 个拓扑推导 ASV 表达式并做 MC 验证。\n      Monotonicity 和 sharpness 作为 conjecture + numerical evidence，不要求 formal proof。\n    expected_results:\n      mbias_monotonicity_mc: \"holds (0/1000 violations)\"\n      mbias_sharpness_mc: \"not achieved — bound conservative by 1.6–2.1x\"\n      mbias_coverage_95: 0.86\n      instrument_monotonicity_mc: \"holds (0/1000 violations)\"\n      instrument_sharpness_mc: \"near-sharp — within 1.1x in 3% of scenarios\"\n      instrument_coverage_95: 0.88\n      frontdoor_monotonicity_mc: \"holds for 97% of scenarios (3% violations at extreme C)\"\n      frontdoor_sharpness_mc: \"not achieved — bound conservative by 1.8–2.4x\"\n      frontdoor_coverage_95: 0.76\n      aggregate_coverage_95_all_6: 0.85\n    result_rationale: |\n      M-bias 的 monotonicity 成立因为 M-bias 的 bias 结构本质上是两条 confounding path 的\n      叠加——每条 path 的 bias 对 δ 单调，叠加后仍单调。但 sharpness 不成立因为\n      两条 path 的 maximum bias 不能同时达到——worst-case C 对 path 1 最优时，\n      对 path 2 不一定最优，dual-confounder 结构限制了 joint worst case 的可达性。\n\n      Instrument 的 monotonicity 成立因为 IV estimation 的 bias 在 instrument misclassification\n      下是线性的——Wald estimator 的分母（first-stage coefficient）被 attenuation，\n      bias = true_effect × (1 - attenuation_factor)，monotone in δ。Near-sharp 因为\n      IV 的 linear structure 使 bound 很接近 achievable maximum。\n\n      Front-door 有 3% violations 因为 front-door criterion 涉及两步：(1) exposure → mediator\n      和 (2) mediator → outcome（调整 exposure）。在极端 C 下（near-rank-deficient），\n      步骤 (2) 的调整不稳定——small δ change 可能 flip 步骤 (2) 的调整方向，\n      导致总 bias 的 local non-monotonicity。这是 compound estimation 的固有问题，\n      与 collider 的 non-monotonicity 机制不同（collider 是 conditioning 问题，front-door 是\n      调整稳定性问题）。\n\n      Aggregate coverage 0.85：front-door 的 0.76 拉低整体。如果排除 front-door，\n      remaining 5 topologies 的 mean coverage 是 0.87。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: ASV Validation Summary — Remaining 3 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          3 rows × columns: topology, monotonicity_status, violation_rate,\n          sharpness_status, bound_tightness, coverage_90/95/99.\n          附注释解释 front-door 3% violations 的机制。\n      - name: \"Table 12: Aggregate ASV Framework Status — All 6 Topologies\"\n        description: |\n          综合 Table 9 和 Table 11 的 summary view。6 rows，每行标注\n          proof_type (formal / MC-conjecture) 和 overall_status (full / partial / needs-repair)。\n          Color-coded: confounding=green, mediation/instrument/mbias=yellow,\n          collider/frontdoor=orange。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: ASV(δ) curves for M-bias/instrument/front-door，与 Fig 10 对应。Instrument curves 最 clean（几乎线性），front-door 有 2-3 条 curves 在极端 C 下出现微弱 non-monotonicity。\"\n    analysis: |\n      5/6 拓扑 monotonicity 基本成立（collider 7% violations + front-door 3% violations\n      是仅有的例外）。从论文叙事角度，这支持 \"ASV 框架在大多数实用场景下有效\" 的 claim，\n      但 \"大多数\" 而非 \"所有\" 是 worst 档的定义性特征。Sharpness 普遍不足——\n      6 个拓扑中仅 confounding 达到 formal sharpness，instrument 接近。\n      这意味着 ASV 在实践中偏 conservative（报告的 robustness 比实际更悲观），\n      对 practitioners 来说是 safe 的方向但削弱了 ASV 的 \"precision\" selling point。\n      Version B framing 将 ASV 定位为 \"magnitude uncertainty 的 robustness measure\"\n      而非 \"direction reversal 的 guard\"——这个定位与 sharpness 不足是兼容的\n      （magnitude uncertainty 不需要 tight bound，conservative 即可）。\n\n  - name: \"ASV empirical calibration (3 tasks × 3 LLMs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: |\n      将 ASV 应用到 plan_003 的经验混淆矩阵，在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage，\n      报告 ASV alongside downstream effect estimates。\n    expected_results:\n      meaningful_asv_count: 4\n      vacuous_asv_count: 5\n      concordance_meaningful: \"4/4 (all meaningful ASVs correctly classify robust vs fragile)\"\n      concordance_total: \"4/9 (5 vacuous cases are trivially correct but uninformative)\"\n      empirical_asv_concordance: 4\n      asv_infinite_or_very_large_cases: 5\n      protest_Qwen_asv: \"finite, ASV=2.3 (fragile)\"\n      protest_Llama_asv: \"finite, ASV=4.1 (moderate)\"\n      stance_DeepSeek_asv: \"large, ASV=18.7 (robust)\"\n      toxicity_all_asv: \">50 (robust, binary special case)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      经验混淆矩阵 diagonal-dominant（plan_003 结果），因此达到 direction-reversing 或\n      magnitude-significant 的 δ threshold 很高——ASV 值大（甚至无穷）。\n      5/9 combinations 的 ASV ≫10，意味着 \"需要当前 annotation error 放大 10 倍以上\n      才会产生有意义的 bias\"——technically correct 但 uninformative（研究者已经知道\n      高准确率 LLM 产生的 bias 小）。4/9 meaningful cases 出现在 K=5 protest event coding\n      （准确率最低，off-diagonal mass 最大）和 K=3 stance detection 与较弱模型的组合。\n      这些 meaningful cases 中 ASV 正确区分了 fragile（ASV<5）vs robust（ASV>10）——\n      但样本量太小（4 cases）无法做统计检验。\n\n      Worst 档的核心困境在此体现：ASV 的理论价值依赖于经验 C 足够 \"interesting\"，\n      但 SOTA LLMs 太好了，经验 C 太 \"boring\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: ASV Values — 9 Combinations\"\n        description: |\n          9 rows × columns: task, model, K, accuracy, diagonal_dominance,\n          ASV_value, ASV_classification (fragile/moderate/robust),\n          held_out_bias, held_out_direction, concordance (✓/✗/trivial).\n          5 行标注 \"trivial\" (ASV>50)，4 行标注 ✓。\n      - name: \"Table 14: ASV vs Raw Confusion Matrix — Interpretability Comparison\"\n        description: |\n          对 4 个 meaningful cases，并排展示 ASV summary 和 raw confusion matrix，\n          说明 ASV 提供了哪些 confusion matrix 本身不直接给出的信息\n          （主要是 \"离 danger zone 有多远\" 的距离度量）。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 13: ASV sensitivity curve — 对 protest/Qwen (ASV=2.3) case，画 bias magnitude as function of δ amplification factor。Vertical line at δ=1 (current error)，δ=2.3 处 bias crosses significance threshold。展示 ASV 的可视化解读。\"\n      - \"Fig 14: ASV distribution across 9 combinations — dot plot with log scale y axis。Clear separation between 4 finite-meaningful (ASV 2-5) and 5 vacuous (ASV >15) cases。\"\n    analysis: |\n      4/9 concordance 在 [3,6] 范围的低端。论文叙事需要将这个结果 reframe：\n      不是 \"ASV 在 9 个场景中只有 4 个有用\"，而是 \"ASV 正确识别了 4 个值得关注的\n      high-risk combinations——这些是研究者在没有 ASV 的情况下可能忽略的\"。\n      对 5 个 vacuous cases，论文可以说 \"ASV 为这些 combinations 提供了 formal robustness\n      guarantee，研究者可以安心使用\"——但 reviewer 可能反驳 \"any reasonable researcher\n      wouldn't worry about a 85%-accurate annotator\"。\n\n      增强策略：(a) semi-synthetic 注入——在经验 C 上添加 controlled degradation\n      （accuracy 从 0.8 降至 0.5），展示 ASV 如何从 \"robust\" 转变为 \"fragile\"，\n      (b) 增加低资源任务（如小语种情感分析 K=7），提高观察到 meaningful ASV 的概率，\n      (c) user study——给研究者展示 ASV vs 不展示 ASV，测量决策质量差异。\n\n  - name: \"Correction guidance framework\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: |\n      构建 {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction method 的决策框架，\n      MC 验证 recommended method 在 ≥90% scenarios 产生最小 bias，\n      经验数据验证。\n    expected_results:\n      overall_accuracy: 0.78\n      mla_recommendation_fraction: 0.65\n      exposure_reversal_recommendation: \"gold label collection / no adequate correction\"\n      exposure_accuracy: 0.85\n      confounding_accuracy: 0.82\n      collider_accuracy: 0.68\n      scenarios_where_no_method_adequate: 0.12\n      ppi_outperforms_mla_fraction: 0.08\n      dsl_applicable_fraction: 0.05\n      naive_plugin_never_recommended: true\n      correction_framework_accuracy: 0.78\n      decision_tree_depth: 4\n      decision_tree_leaf_purity: 0.73\n    result_rationale: |\n      Correction framework accuracy 0.78 反映了 worst 档的核心预测：framework 在多数场景\n      退化为 \"use MLA\"。当 65% 的 scenarios 的最优推荐是 MLA 时，一个 trivial baseline\n      \"always recommend MLA\" 就有 65% accuracy——framework 的 0.78 仅比 trivial baseline\n      高 13 个百分点，discriminative value 有限。\n\n      MLA 主导的原因：MLA (Measurement-error Likelihood Adjustment) 是最 general 的方法，\n      它利用 C 矩阵估计对 likelihood 做调整，适用于任何 topology + 任何 error structure。\n      在 5 个 \"well-behaved\" topology（方向可预测）中，MLA 几乎总是最优选择因为它直接\n      纠正 bias magnitude。PPI 仅在 finite-sample regime（small gold sample + large LLM sample）\n      优于 MLA（8% scenarios）。DSL 仅在 very specific conditions（已知 C + linear model）下\n      优于 MLA（5% scenarios）。\n\n      Exposure topology 是 framework 最有价值的部分——对 reversal-risk scenarios，framework\n      正确推荐 \"no correction adequate without gold labels\"，这是 non-trivial guidance\n      （naive researcher 可能尝试 MLA 但 MLA 在 sign-reversed regime 可能 amplify error）。\n\n      Collider accuracy 最低（0.68）因为 collider bias correction 依赖于 conditioning strategy——\n      \"correct the annotation then re-condition\" vs \"don't condition at all\" 的选择\n      取决于 effect magnitude 和 C structure 的交互，decision tree 难以准确捕获。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Correction Guidance Decision Framework\"\n        description: |\n          Matrix format: rows = topologies (6), columns = error structure categories\n          (diagonal-dominant / moderate / near-permutation × differential / non-differential),\n          cells = recommended method + ASV threshold. 大量 cells 填入 \"MLA\"。\n          Exposure 行的 near-permutation cells 标红 \"gold labels required\"。\n      - name: \"Table 16: Framework Accuracy — MC Validation\"\n        description: |\n          Per topology accuracy, per error-structure accuracy, confusion matrix of\n          {recommended method × actually-best method}. 最大 off-diagonal cluster:\n          MLA recommended but PPI actually marginally better (差异 <0.01 bias)。\n      - name: \"Table 17: Open Problem Identification\"\n        description: |\n          12% of scenarios 标记为 \"no existing method adequate\"。\n          Columns: scenario_description, why_inadequate, required_capability.\n          主要集中在 differential multi-class error + complex topology (M-bias, front-door)\n          和 correlated multi-LLM error。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 15: Decision tree visualization — depth 4, 12 leaves。Color = recommended method。大量绿色叶节点（MLA），少量红色（gold labels）和蓝色（PPI）。视觉上展示 'MLA 主导' 的现实。\"\n      - \"Fig 16: Framework accuracy vs ASV — scatter plot，x = ASV magnitude，y = framework recommendation correct (1/0)。低 ASV（fragile）区域 accuracy 更高（framework 更有价值），高 ASV（robust）区域 accuracy 无意义（任何推荐都 work）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Correction framework 在 worst 档下的 selling point 不是 accuracy 而是 completeness——\n      \"first systematic mapping of when each correction method applies, with identified open problems\"。\n      0.78 accuracy 加上 MLA 65% dominance 意味着 framework 的 practical value 集中在\n      ~35% non-MLA scenarios（exposure reversal + PPI edge cases + no-method-adequate regimes）。\n      Version B narrative 中 Claim 3 权重增加，需要将 framework 包装为 \"practitioner's guide\"\n      而非 \"automated decision system\"——降低 accuracy 期望，强调 \"the framework identifies\n      what you should worry about, not just what to do\"。\n      Open problems 部分（12% no-method-adequate）可能是最有 citation value 的贡献——\n      明确指出 correlated multi-LLM error correction 是 unsolved problem，引导后续研究。\n\n  - name: \"Pathological confusion matrix analysis (spectral)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: |\n      分析极端 C 结构（near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal）在 6 个拓扑下的\n      bias 行为，用 spectral 分析（eigenvalue spectrum of C）识别 bias severity 的\n      structural predictors。\n    expected_results:\n      exposure_reversal_spectral_threshold: \"λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 for K=3\"\n      exposure_reversal_prediction_auc: 0.92\n      diagonal_dominance_as_simple_predictor: \"reversal when diag_dom < 0.45\"\n      diagonal_dominance_prediction_auc: 0.89\n      other_topologies_spectral_finding: \"monotone relationship between λ₁ and bias magnitude; no reversal threshold exists\"\n      spectral_gap_predicts_magnitude_R2: 0.78\n      block_diagonal_C_magnitude_effect: \"1.5–2.3x bias amplification vs random C of same accuracy\"\n      rank_deficient_C_behavior: \"bias expressions numerically unstable, need regularization\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Exposure DAG 的反转机制有清晰的 spectral interpretation：C 矩阵的 eigendecomposition\n      中，λ₁ 对应 \"correct classification\" mode（沿 identity 方向），λ₂ 对应 \"dominant confusion\"\n      mode（label swap 方向）。当 λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 时，confusion mode 足够强以翻转 treatment\n      assignment 的有效方向，产生 sign reversal。这个阈值在 K=3 下给出 AUC 0.92 的\n      reversal 预测——spectral gap 是一个 principled predictor。\n      Diagonal dominance（diag_dom = min_i C_ii / max_i Σ_{j≠i} C_ij）是更简单的 proxy，\n      AUC 0.89 略低但更直观。\n\n      对其余 5 个拓扑，spectral 分析揭示 λ₁ 与 bias magnitude 的 monotone relationship\n      （R²=0.78），但没有 \"reversal threshold\"——bias 方向由 topology 的结构性质决定\n      （confounding → toward OVB, mediation → toward attenuation, etc.），C 的 spectrum\n      只调制 magnitude。这在理论上不意外（worst 档假设），但提供了一个\n      compact characterization。\n\n      Block-diagonal C（如 K=6 分成两个 K=3 block，block 间无混淆）产生 1.5-2.3x\n      bias amplification 因为 block 结构创造了 \"structured confusion\"——模型在 block 内\n      混淆但 block 间清晰，这比同等 accuracy 的 random C 产生更大 bias\n      因为 confusion 集中而非分散。\n\n      Rank-deficient C 导致某些 bias 表达式的矩阵求逆不稳定——这是实际计算中的\n      nuisance，不是理论 insight，但需要在 toolkit 中处理（regularization）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 18: Spectral Predictors of Bias Severity\"\n        description: |\n          Columns: predictor (λ₂/λ₁, diag_dom, spectral_gap, Frobenius_norm),\n          target (reversal_binary, bias_magnitude), topology, AUC_or_R².\n          Exposure rows 有 reversal prediction AUC，其余行仅有 magnitude R²。\n      - name: \"Table 19: Pathological C Structure Catalog\"\n        description: |\n          Catalog of 4 pathological C types × 6 topologies × {bias_magnitude,\n          direction_preserved, numerical_stability}。27 行 summary。\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 17: Spectral gap vs bias — 2 panels。Left: exposure DAG，scatter with reversal colored red/blue，clear threshold at λ₂/λ₁=0.6。Right: confounding DAG，smooth monotone curve，no threshold。最直观的 'dichotomy' spectral evidence。\"\n      - \"Fig 18: Block-diagonal C amplification — bar chart comparing bias from block-diagonal vs random C at matched accuracy, across 6 topologies。展示 structured confusion 的 amplification effect。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Spectral 分析在 worst 档下提供了 exposure 反转的 mechanistic explanation——\n      这是 narrative 需要的 \"deep dive\"。λ₂/λ₁ > 0.6 threshold 是一个 actionable\n      practitioner guideline（\"检查你的 confusion matrix 的 spectral gap，如果 < 0.4\n      则 exposure 标注安全\"）。对其余拓扑，spectral 分析的贡献更 modest——\n      确认了 \"方向可预测，magnitude 依赖 C\" 的结论但没有 surprising insight。\n      Block-diagonal 发现是 bonus 内容——在 CSS 中，block-diagonal C 对应\n      \"模型区分粗粒度类别但混淆细粒度类别\" 的常见模式，有实际意义。\n      建议在论文中将 spectral 分析作为 Section 4 的 highlight（exposure deep dive），\n      其余拓扑的 spectral 结果放 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"annot-sensitivity Python toolkit\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: |\n      Open-source Python 包：用户输入 DAG + confusion matrix + downstream estimate →\n      输出 bias expressions + ASV bounds + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation\n      + diagnostic plots。pip-installable，每个 topology 一个 worked example。\n    expected_results:\n      pip_installable: true\n      supported_topologies: 6\n      K_range_supported: \"2–15\"\n      runtime_K3: \"<0.1s\"\n      runtime_K7: \"<1s\"\n      runtime_K15: \"<10s\"\n      worked_examples: 6\n      api_surface: \"BiasExpr, ASV, CorrectionGuide, DiagnosticPlot\"\n      test_coverage: \"~85%\"\n      documentation_pages: \"~20\"\n      demo_value_assessment: \"limited by diagonal-dominant empirical C\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Toolkit 是 engineering deliverable 而非实验。在 worst 档下，toolkit 本身功能完整\n      但 demonstration value 受限：经验混淆矩阵太 diagonal-dominant，toolkit 在 demo 中\n      主要输出 \"your annotation is fine\"——不够 compelling 作为 conference demo。\n      Worked examples 需要用 semi-synthetic C 而非 pure empirical C 来展示\n      toolkit 的 full capability（包括 reversal detection, ASV fragility warning, etc.）。\n      Runtime 快（K≤7 < 1s）因为 bias expressions 是 closed-form matrix operations，\n      不需要 MC simulation。K=15 需要 ~10s 因为 15×15 矩阵的 eigendecomposition\n      和 worst-case optimization 增加计算量。\n      作为 Claim 3 (\"correction guidance\") 的 tangible artifact，toolkit 增加论文的\n      practical impact——即使理论贡献在 worst 档下被削弱，一个 pip-installable tool\n      是 reviewer 认可的 concrete contribution。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 19: Toolkit workflow diagram — input (DAG graph + C matrix + β̂) → 4 outputs (bias expression + ASV + sensitivity curve + correction recommendation)。展示 API 的 end-to-end flow。\"\n      - \"Fig 20: Toolkit screenshot — 对 protest/Qwen case (ASV=2.3) 的实际输出截图，包括 sensitivity curve plot 和 correction recommendation。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Toolkit 在 worst 档下是 \"保底贡献\"——即使 taxonomy 不够 dramatic、ASV 有 coverage 问题、\n      correction framework 主要推荐 MLA，一个 well-documented open-source tool 仍有独立价值。\n      建议在论文中给 toolkit 一个 dedicated subsection（不只是 \"code available at github\"），\n      展示 API 设计和 worked examples。在 supplementary material 中包含\n      comprehensive tutorial notebook。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dd93169f-899b-425b-835b-3968c6801b13","total_cost_usd":0.7131967499999999,"